===Television series===
{{main|A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms (TV series) {{!}} ''A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms'' (TV series)}}
Martin wrote in 2014 that film or TV adaptations of the novellas were being discussed. He suggested that because [[HBO]] owns the TV rights to the setting of Westeros (if not to the characters of the novellas), it would be preferable to have HBO adapt the novellas as well.<ref name="Not a Blog 2014-04"/> On January 21, 2021, ''[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]'' reported that an adaptation of the ''Tales of Dunk and Egg'' series, a prequel to the events of ''[[Game of Thrones]]'', was in early development on HBO.<ref name=Variety>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/game-of-thrones-tales-of-dunk-and-egg-series-hbo-1234889520/|title='Game of Thrones' Prequel 'Tales of Dunk and Egg' in Early Development at HBO (EXCLUSIVE)|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|first=Joe|last=Otterson|date=January 21, 2021|access-date=January 21, 2021|archive-date=January 21, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210121195155/https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/game-of-thrones-tales-of-dunk-and-egg-series-hbo-1234889520/|url-status=live}}</ref> It was given a straight to series order on April 12, 2023.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/game-of-thrones-prequel-series-a-knight-of-the-seven-kingdoms-hbo-1235578466/ |title='Game of Thrones' Prequel Series 'A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms: The Hedge Knight' Ordered at HBO |author=Otterson, Joe |publisher=Variety |date=April 12, 2023 |accessdate=April 12, 2023 |archive-date=April 12, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230412182554/https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/game-of-thrones-prequel-series-a-knight-of-the-seven-kingdoms-hbo-1235578466/ |url-status=live }}</ref>  The show stars [[Peter Claffey]] and [[Dexter Sol Ansell]] as Dunk and Egg, respectively.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/game-of-thrones-prequel-hedge-knight-knight-of-the-seven-kingdoms-cast-peter-claffey-dexter-sol-ansell-1235961895/ |title='Game of Thrones' Prequel 'Knight of the Seven Kingdoms: The Hedge Knight' Casts Peter Claffey, Dexter Sol Ansell in Lead Roles |author=Otterson, Joe |publisher=Variety |date=April 5, 2024}}</ref> Filming began in [[Belfast]], [[Northern Ireland]] in June 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Vary |first=Adam B. |date=June 18, 2024 |title=''Game of Thrones'' Spinoff ''A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms'' Begins Filming as ''The Crown, True Detective'' Actors Join Cast |url=https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/game-of-thrones-knight-of-the-seven-kingdoms-production-1236041563/ |access-date=June 18, 2024 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref> The series premiered on January 18, 2026, on [[HBO]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=White |first1=Abbey |last2=Hibberd |first2=James |date=October 9, 2025 |title=''A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms'': First Trailer for ''Game of Thrones'' Spinoff Drops |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/knight-of-the-seven-kingdoms-game-of-thrones-trailer-hbo-1236396048/ |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |access-date=December 6, 2025}}</ref> The first season covers the events of the first novella, ''[[#The Hedge Knight|The Hedge Knight]]'', while a second season has been confirmed, which will be based on ''[[#The Sworn Sword|The Sworn Sword]]'' and is expected to be released in 2027.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hibberd |first=James |date=January 17, 2026 |title=George R.R. Martin Handed ''Seven Kingdoms'' Showrunner 12 Unpublished Dunk and Egg Stories |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/knight-of-the-seven-kingdoms-interview-1236471682/ |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260117163750/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/knight-of-the-seven-kingdoms-interview-1236471682/ |archive-date=January 17, 2026 |access-date=January 30, 2026}}</ref>

